 2 │ 
 3 │ Ledgerline, our hypothetical Python ORM library, is built with performance as a core design principle.  A significant component of achieving this is its robust caching layer, designed to dramatically reduce database load and improve response times for common queries. This overview will detail how the caching mechanism operates within Ledgerline, focusing on query result caching, cache invalidation strategies, and the distinctions between request-level and process-level scopes.
