 41 │ 
 42 │ The Metadata Cache plays a crucial supporting role. It stores information *about* the cached query results – primarily the last accessed time and the SQL query itself. This allows Ledgerline to efficiently determine when a cache entry is stale (based on its TTL) and to quickly identify which queries need to be re-executed if an invalidation occurs.
